// Generated by build.js. Do not edit.
module.exports = { KB: [{"always":true,"t":"About MpxHR","x":"MpxHR Enterprise 4.2.0 is an offline HR, attendance and payroll desktop application for 64-bit Windows 10 and 11. Data stays on the user's own computer. No monthly cloud fee. Internet is needed only for optional email and Google Sync. Every plan includes every feature. 14-day free trial (up to 50 employees), no card needed."},{"always":true,"t":"Contact and support","x":"Contact Mithlesh Prasad on WhatsApp 7519024725 or email mithleshprasad58@gmail.com. Support in Hindi and English. Help available with installation, importing employee and attendance data from Excel, and training."},{"t":"Download and install","x":"Download the Windows installer (about 110 MB) from the Download page. Run it; if Windows shows Unknown publisher click More info then Run anyway. Open MpxHR, sign in, and the 14-day trial starts automatically. Requirements: Windows 10 or 11 64-bit, 4 GB RAM recommended, about 500 MB free disk."},{"t":"Employee management","x":"Complete employee records with photo, signature, documents, custom fields, departments, designations and branches."},{"t":"Attendance & shifts","x":"Daily and monthly attendance, shifts, Excel import for many months at once, and a clear present/absent summary."},{"t":"Payroll with flexible salary heads","x":"Any number of earning and deduction heads, PF, ESI, TDS, loans, bulk edits and a Net Pay sheet you can trust."},{"t":"Payslips & Payslip Designer","x":"Professional payslips with your logo, amount in words and a drag-and-drop designer for your own layout."},{"t":"Dashboard & analytics","x":"Live headcount, attendance, payroll and department charts for every company at a glance."},{"t":"Reports & Form 16","x":"Ready-made reports, Form 16 and a custom report builder. Export to Excel or PDF in a click."},{"t":"Letters & email","x":"Offer letters, experience letters and more from templates. Email payslips and letters to employees automatically."},{"t":"Google Sync & Forms","x":"Export tables to Google Sheets, import rows through an approval queue and build Google Forms that fill several tables."},{"t":"Photo, signature & document intake","x":"Add files one by one or in bulk from a folder, Excel sheet or Google Drive, with your own size and type limits."},{"t":"Secure by design","x":"Roles and module rights, lock-out after wrong passwords, master recovery password, backups and restore."},{"t":"100% offline","x":"Your data stays on your computer. No monthly cloud fee, no internet needed for daily work."},{"t":"Onboarding & Joiner Form","x":"A joining checklist for every new joiner, a link they fill from their phone with documents, and one-click Make Employee."},{"t":"Reliable backups","x":"Data and documents in one file, optional password, automatic backup on exit, and restore with a safety copy."},{"t":"Custom fields & tables","x":"Add your own fields to forms or create new tables with no coding."},{"t":"Does MpxHR need the internet?","x":"No. Daily work (employees, attendance, payroll, payslips, reports) is fully offline and your data stays on your computer. The internet is used only by the optional Email and Google Sync features, and nothing is ever sent to us."},{"t":"What happens after the 14-day trial?","x":"You enter the license key from us and carry on with all your data intact. Without a key the app switches to view-only mode: you can still view, print and export everything, but cannot add or change records until a key is entered."},{"t":"What is the difference between the yearly plans and Lifetime?","x":"Yearly plans (Starter, Business, Enterprise, CA / Consultant) run until a date and are renewed with a new key. After a yearly plan ends there is a 15-day grace period. Lifetime is a one-time payment with no expiry date and no employee or company limit."},{"t":"How does the license key work?","x":"The key is a signed text code. You paste it in Settings › License and it is checked on your computer, with no internet needed. It is not tied to one computer, so you can move the software to a new PC and re-enter the same key."},{"t":"Can I upgrade later if I add more employees?","x":"Yes. Ask us and we issue a new key with the higher limit. Your data stays as it is. Renewals simply extend the date."},{"t":"Is my data safe?","x":"Data is stored in a database file on your computer. You can take backups at any time, restore them, protect access with roles and passwords, and use the master recovery password if an admin password is lost."},{"t":"Which Windows versions are supported?","x":"MpxHR runs on 64-bit Windows 10 and Windows 11."},{"t":"Why does Windows say \"Unknown publisher\" when I install?","x":"The installer is not yet signed with a paid code-signing certificate, so Windows shows this notice for any new software. Click \"More info\" and then \"Run anyway\". The file is the one you received from us."},{"t":"Can you set it up for us and train our staff?","x":"Yes. We can help with installation, importing your employee and attendance data from Excel, and a short training session. Contact us on WhatsApp."},{"t":"Can I import my existing data?","x":"Yes. Employees and attendance import from Excel with a preview and validation before anything is saved. Photos, signatures and documents import from a folder, Excel or Google Drive."},{"t":"How to: Install and log in for the first time","x":"Run the MpxHR installer you received and follow the screens (Windows may show \"Unknown publisher\": click More info then Run anyway ). Start MpxHR Enterprise from the desktop icon. Sign in with the user name and password given to you. Tick Remember my user name if you like; use the eye icon to show the password. After 5 wrong attempts the login pauses for 30 seconds (doubling each time up to 15 minutes), so wait and try again. Pick your company on the next screen to open the dashboard."},{"t":"How to: Set up your company, branches and departments","x":"Open Masters › Companies . The General tab holds the name, code, address and logo (the logo prints on payslips); the Statutory, PF / ESI and Bank tabs hold PAN, TAN, GSTIN, PF and ESI details. Add Branches , Departments and Designations from the Masters ribbon. Open Masters › Settings to check Payroll & Leave rules and Module Rights. Create extra logins for other staff under Settings › Security & Users ."},{"t":"How to: Add employees, one by one or from Excel","x":"Open Masters › Employees and click Add . Fill in the employee code, name, joining date and salary structure. Use the Photo and Signature browse buttons; the picture is checked against your limits and resized if very large. For many employees click Template , fill the Excel sheet and click Import . Read the preview: errors and warnings are listed (duplicate codes, unreadable dates and so on). Nothing is saved until you confirm."},{"t":"How to: Bulk-upload photos, signatures and documents","x":"In Employees click Import Files and choose a source: local folder , Excel sheet or Google Drive . Name files after the employee code, for example EMP001.jpg (photo), EMP001_signature.png or EMP001_Aadhaar.pdf . Click Preview to see every file with the employee it matches and anything that will be skipped. Click Import . Set the size and file-type limits in Settings › Files & Uploads ."},{"t":"How to: Mark and import attendance","x":"Open Attendance › Monthly Attn. : every employee against every day as a colour-coded grid (P, A, L, WO, HD, PL, HL). Click a cell to change it. Use Mark Multiple to give one status to several employees over a date range, or Auto-Fill to mark the remaining blank days Present before payroll. To load many days at once click Tpl for the Excel layout, fill it and click Imp . One file can hold several months. The preview checks unknown employee codes, bad dates and duplicate employee + date pairs before anything is saved."},{"t":"How to: Manage leave requests","x":"Open Attendance › Leave App. and define leave types (with a yearly maximum) and the holiday calendar. Choose the employee, leave type, dates and reason and submit. An administrator approves or rejects. Balances are tracked automatically, and the employee can be emailed the decision if Email is set up."},{"t":"How to: Run payroll and review Net Pay","x":"Open Payroll › Net Pay and confirm the Company, Financial Year and Month in the top context bar. Click the refresh icon to calculate from attendance and the salary structure. PF, VPF, ESI, Professional Tax, TDS, loan EMI and your own deductions are applied automatically. Click any row to see its full detail, or tick employees and use Bulk Update Head to set or add one salary head for all of them (or import the amounts from Excel). Click Save to commit the payroll, then Export to Excel, or use Challan for the PF/ESI/PT/TDS deposit summary."},{"t":"How to: Create and email payslips","x":"Open Payroll › Payslips , which lists every processed payslip for the period. Click a row to preview it. The payslip shows your logo, income and deduction heads, loan details and amount in words. Choose Download PDF , Download Word or Print . Tick many employees for the Bulk Export Wizard (one ZIP). Tick employees and click Email Selected to mail each their payslip as a PDF (set up Email first). Use Masters › Payslip Designer to design your own layout."},{"t":"How to: Reports, Form 16 and letters","x":"Open Reports and choose a ready-made report such as the salary sheet, PF/ESI statement or attendance summary. Use Form 16 for the employee tax certificate. Build your own with the Custom Report Builder . In Documents choose a letter template, pick the employee and print or email it. Use the Signature (image) tag to place the signature."},{"t":"How to: Set up email (Gmail, Outlook, Zoho ...)","x":"Open Masters › Settings › Email and choose your provider (Gmail SMTP, Outlook, Zoho, Yahoo, any SMTP server or a Google account). For Gmail create an App Password in your Google account security page and paste it instead of the normal password. Send a test email, then edit the templates for payslip, letter, leave and birthday mails."},{"t":"How to: Connect Google Sheets and Forms","x":"Open Settings › Google Sync › Connect a Sheet and copy the script shown. Paste it into Google Apps Script, deploy it as a web app and paste the web-app URL back in MpxHR. Export a table to the sheet, or import rows; imported rows wait in a Review Queue until you approve them. Use the Form Builder to create a Google Form whose answers fill several tables at once."},{"t":"How to: Onboard a new joiner with the Joiner Form","x":"Open Masters › Onboarding and click New Joiner . A joining checklist is created for the person. Click Joiner Form › Questions & documents and tick what the joiner should fill in and upload. Mark compulsory ones as Must fill . Click Get link / Share . The first time, follow the short guide to paste the script into your Google Sheet, then press Check now . Send the link by WhatsApp or email. Click View responses to see what came in, then Add new joiners to bring them and their documents into MpxHR. Select a joiner and click Make Employee . The details, photo, signature and documents are copied; open Employees to add the code and salary."},{"t":"How to: Enter your license key","x":"Open Masters › Settings › License (near the top of the list) or click the license chip in the top bar. Paste the key you received from us and click Activate . The page shows your plan, employee and company limits and the expiry date. To renew or upgrade just enter the new key; your data is untouched."},{"t":"How to: Back up and restore your data","x":"Open Masters › Settings › Database Maintenance . Choose Everything (data + documents) or Data only ; a password can encrypt a data-only backup. The card at the top shows when you last backed up. Tick Back up automatically every time I close MpxHR , choose a folder (a Google Drive or OneDrive folder gives an off-site copy) and how many backups to keep. To restore click Choose a backup file , or Restore on a recent automatic backup. A safety copy of your current data is saved first and MpxHR restarts afterwards. If an admin password is lost, use the master recovery password set in Settings › Security & Users ."},{"t":"Plan Starter (Small teams)","x":"Price ₹5,600 / year excluding GST. Up to 25 employees. 1 company. All features included. Email and WhatsApp support."},{"t":"Plan Business (Growing companies)","x":"Price ₹16,000 / year excluding GST. Up to 100 employees. 1 company. All features included. Email and WhatsApp support."},{"t":"Plan Enterprise (Large organisations)","x":"Price on request (ask for a quote on WhatsApp). Unlimited employees. Unlimited companies. All features included. Priority support."},{"t":"Plan CA / Consultant (Handle many clients' payroll)","x":"Price on request (ask for a quote on WhatsApp). Unlimited employees. Several companies (as agreed). Separate data per company. Priority support."},{"t":"Plan Lifetime (Pay once, use forever)","x":"Price ₹32,000 one-time excluding GST. Unlimited employees. Unlimited companies. No expiry date. All features included."},{"t":"Release 4.2.0 (2026-10-04)","x":"New Onboarding module: joining checklist for every new joiner, printable joining form and one-click Make Employee. Joiner Form: send a link, new joiners fill details and upload documents from a phone. Pick any questions, with checks and file-size limits, then review and add the answers. Reliable backups: always the real database, verified after saving, encrypted option, keep the newest N, and restore with a safety copy. Fixes backups that missed the database in installed copies of 4.1.x. New look for every list: summary cards, avatars and status pills on Employees, Attendance, Payroll, Payslips, Loans and the masters; redesigned Salary Sheet with a totals row. Settings menu scrolls, Logout is never cut off, and Google Forms have Preview, Share and a guided setup."},{"t":"Release 4.1.2 (2026-10-02)","x":"A license chip is always visible in the top bar, so the plan and days left are never hidden. License moved near the top of the Settings list."},{"t":"Release 4.1.1 (2026-10-02)","x":"One Signature box on the employee form (older custom signature fields are merged automatically)."},{"t":"Guide: What's New in Version 4.2","x":"This guide covers everything in MpxHR up to version 4.2. The highlights of 4.2 come first, then the earlier 4.x highlights: Onboarding A joining checklist for every new joiner before an employee record exists, a printable joining form, and Make Employee in one click. (Section 22) Joiner Form Send a link; new joiners fill their details and upload documents from a phone. Choose any question, with checks and file limits, review the answers, then add them. (Section 22) Reliable backups Backups now always capture the database the program really uses, are checked after saving, keep the newest N, and restore with a safety copy. (Section 19) New look for every list Summary cards, avatars, chips and status pills on Employees, Attendance, Payroll, Payslips, Loans and the masters, plus a redesigned Salary Sheet with a totals row. (Section 4, 9) Flexible salary structure Every employee can now have "},{"t":"Guide: What's New in Version 4.2 / Smaller improvements","x":"Settings menu now scrolls, so Custom Fields, Files & Uploads, Security & Users and Module Rights can be reached on a laptop screen; the top-bar Logout button is no longer cut off on narrow windows. Google Forms in the Form Builder have Preview and Share (copy, WhatsApp, email), and a short guided setup wizard with a \"Check now\" button for the one-time Google script update. When a window opens over another (Share, Preview), the one underneath is tucked away until you close it. Employee and Net Pay rows open full detail with a single click anywhere on the row - no need to tick the checkbox first. The Financial Year dropdown now generates itself (current year 4 to +1) and always selects today's year. Page changes show a small spinner on the clicked button instead of a full-screen loader. Attendance import handles several months in one file and shows a result summary per month. Salary Head s"},{"t":"Guide: 1. Introduction & Overview","x":"MpxHR Enterprise is a complete, offline-first Desktop HR Management System for small and mid-sized organisations. It runs on a local computer - no internet is needed for day-to-day use - and keeps all company, employee, attendance and payroll data on that machine. Internet is only used by the optional features: Email and Google Sync."},{"t":"Guide: 1. Introduction & Overview / What MpxHR manages","x":"Area What it covers Employee Records Personal, statutory (PAN, Aadhaar, PF, ESI, UAN), bank and salary-structure profiles; custom fields Attendance & Leave Daily and monthly attendance, shifts, leave types, holidays, PL/CL credit, Excel import Payroll Automatic PF / VPF / ESI / PT / TDS / loan / custom deductions, bulk head updates, challans Payslips PDF/Word payslips, bulk export, email delivery, custom layout designer Compliance Form 16 certificate, statutory challans, PF/ESI/TDS reports Loans & Assets Employee loans with automatic EMI recovery; asset records (syncable with Google Sheets) Communication NEW Email payslips and letters; automatic leave and birthday emails Integrations NEW Google Sheets sync, Google Form builder Reporting Ready-made reports and a custom report builder Multi-company. One installation can manage several companies and branches. You choose the active company a"},{"t":"Guide: 2. Getting Started / 2.1 Launching and logging in","x":"Double-click the MpxHR icon on the desktop or Start Menu. Enter User Name and Password, then click Sign In . Default administrator login: username admin , password admin123 . Change it immediately after the first login ( Masters > Settings > Security & Users )."},{"t":"Guide: 2. Getting Started / 2.2 Selecting a company","x":"After login the Company Selection screen shows quick numbers (Total Employees, Departments, Present Today, Registered Companies), Quick Reports and the company list. Click a row (or Add to register a new company) and press Continue ."},{"t":"Guide: 2. Getting Started / 2.3 The main window","x":"Area Purpose Context bar (top) Switch Company, Financial Year (Apr Mar) and Month. Most screens filter by these, and reload when you change them. Ribbon tabs Dashboard, Masters, Attendance, Payroll, Reports, Documents Ribbon toolbar Icons for each module of the active tab Title-bar icons Application Tour (magic wand), Keyboard Shortcuts , User Guide (this PDF), Contact Support , Logout Content area The active screen - grids, forms and reports First time here? Click the magic-wand icon for a guided Application Tour of the interface."},{"t":"Guide: 2. Getting Started / 2.4 Ribbon map","x":"Tab Icons Dashboard Overview, Analytics Masters Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches, Salary Heads, Payslip Designer NEW , Categories, Loan Setup, User Deductions, Companies, Data Security, Settings Attendance Daily Attn., Monthly Attn., Leave App., Shifts Payroll Net Pay, Payslips, Loan Setup Reports All Reports Documents Letters"},{"t":"Guide: 3. Dashboard & Analytics / 3.1 Overview","x":"Recently Viewed Pages - quick links back to screens used in this session. Request Links - pending TDS, loan, leave, attendance and reimbursement requests. Bulk Changes Links - jump into bulk-edit mode for Branch, Designation, Employee Details, Salary Definition, Shift or Category. Utility Links - Current Running Loans, EMI Calculator, Section 80C quick reference, Allowance & Deduction shortcuts."},{"t":"Guide: 3. Dashboard & Analytics / 3.2 Analytics","x":"Dashboard > Analytics shows four live charts: Employment Status, Attendance Overview (current month), Salary Distribution by Department and Hiring Growth (last 6 months). Click Refresh Data to reload."},{"t":"Guide: 4. Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches / 4.1 Employees","x":"Masters > Employees is the central record for every staff member. Click anywhere on a row to open the full detail NEW . Adding an employee Click New . Fill personal details (name, DOB, gender, contact, address), employment details (department, designation, date of joining, status), salary structure and statutory numbers: PAN NEW , Aadhaar, PF, ESI, UAN. Fill any custom fields you have defined (Section 17). Add a photo and signature with the Browse buttons beside the form. After the first Save, the Documents box lets you upload Aadhaar, PAN, certificates and so on (Section 14.4). Click Save ( Ctrl + S ). Salary structure. The salary structure is no longer limited to six fixed columns. It lists whichever Salary Heads you define in Masters > Salary Heads , each with its own amount per employee. Editing, selecting, deleting Tick one or more checkboxes (or the header checkbox to select all). "},{"t":"Guide: 4. Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches / 4.2 Departments","x":"Masters > Departments - simple list used for grouping and reporting everywhere."},{"t":"Guide: 4. Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches / 4.3 Designations","x":"Masters > Designations - job titles with a default base salary, LWF Category (Employee / Supervisor / Manager), Probation Period (days) and Deduct PT (whether Professional Tax applies)."},{"t":"Guide: 4. Employees, Departments, Designations, Branches / 4.4 Branches","x":"Masters > Branches - office locations linked to a company; employees and attendance can be filtered by branch."},{"t":"Guide: 5. Salary Heads, Categories, Loans, Deductions / 5.1 Salary Heads UPDATED","x":"Masters > Salary Heads defines every pay component. The grid shows Description, Short Code, Type, Form 16 Purpose and flags for PF, ESI, Bonus, OT and Active. Click Add New , enter the description (for example House Rent Allowance ) and short code. Choose Type : Earning or Deduction (required). Tick whether the head counts toward PF, ESI, Bonus and Overtime, choose its Form 16 purpose, and keep it Active. Save. The head is immediately available in each employee's salary structure, Net Pay, payslips and reports. Use Modify to change a head and Delete to remove one. Existing payroll history keeps working, because older payroll data is read through the same dynamic structure."},{"t":"Guide: 5. Salary Heads, Categories, Loans, Deductions / 5.2 Employee Categories","x":"Masters > Categories - free-form groups (Staff, Worker, Management) for classification and bulk reporting."},{"t":"Guide: 5. Salary Heads, Categories, Loans, Deductions / 5.3 Loan Setup","x":"Masters > Loan Setup (also under the Payroll tab) - record a loan or advance once: Click New ; pick the employee, loan type, principal, monthly EMI and start date. Save. The loan shows as Active with a running balance. Each payroll run deducts the active EMI and reduces the balance. At zero the loan closes automatically; use Mark Closed to close it manually. Loan details also appear on the payslip."},{"t":"Guide: 5. Salary Heads, Categories, Loans, Deductions / 5.4 User Defined Deductions","x":"Masters > User Deductions - company-wide custom deductions (uniform fee, canteen). Each is a Fixed amount or a Percentage of Gross, and applies to every payroll run while Active."},{"t":"Guide: 6. Company & Branch Setup","x":"Masters > Companies holds each company's legal and statutory identity across five tabs: Tab Contents General Name, code, establishment date, business type, address, logo (the logo prints on payslips) Statutory PAN, TAN, GSTIN, CIN, Professional Tax and LWF registration, Tax Circle/CIT PF / ESI PF code, establishment ID, signatory; ESI code, local office, signatory Bank Company bank account for payslips and bank advice Management Two Directors / Authorised Signatories Use Simultaneous Edit to correct several companies at once. A newly added company appears in the top context-bar dropdown immediately, without restarting."},{"t":"Guide: 7. Attendance & Shifts / 7.1 Daily Attendance","x":"Attendance > Daily Attn. - check employees in/out for today or correct a day's punch times and status."},{"t":"Guide: 7. Attendance & Shifts / 7.2 Monthly Attendance","x":"Attendance > Monthly Attn. shows every employee against every day of the month as a colour-coded grid. Click a cell to change it. Code Meaning P Present A Absent L Leave WO Weekly Off HD Half Day PL Paid Leave HL Holiday The PL and RH counters in the header show the remaining Paid Leave and Restricted Holiday balances. Bulk tools Mark Multiple - one status for several employees over a date range. XLS / Tpl / Imp - export the grid, download a fill-in template, or import from Excel. Imports are validated first (Section 14) and can contain several months in one file NEW , with a per-month result summary. Credit Leaves (coins icon) - credits monthly PL/CL to employees who meet tenure and minimum-attendance rules. Auto-Fill (magic wand) - fills remaining blank days as Present before month-end payroll. Restore Default - return a day's cell to its default status."},{"t":"Guide: 7. Attendance & Shifts / 7.3 Shifts","x":"Attendance > Shifts - define shift start/end and grace period, and assign employees through the roster."},{"t":"Guide: 8. Leave Management / 8.1 Applying and approving","x":"Select the employee (administrators only; employees see only their own record), leave type, date range and reason, then submit. An administrator Approves or Rejects . NEW If automatic emails are enabled (Section 15), the employee is emailed the decision."},{"t":"Guide: 8. Leave Management / 8.2 Leave types & holidays","x":"Leave Types - Casual, Sick, Paid Leave etc., each with a yearly maximum and a colour. Holiday Calendar - Public, National or Restricted (RH). Restricted holidays feed the RH balance on the Attendance screen."},{"t":"Guide: 8. Leave Management / 8.3 Leave balances","x":"Running balance per leave type is tracked automatically and visible on the Leave screen and employee profile."},{"t":"Guide: 9. Payroll Processing / 9.1 Payroll months","x":"Each Financial Year / Month has an Open or Closed status. Close a month once payroll is final to prevent accidental changes."},{"t":"Guide: 9. Payroll Processing / 9.2 Generating payroll - Net Pay","x":"Payroll > Net Pay shows every active employee's salary sheet, grouped into Employee Details, Income and Deductions. Click a row to open its full detail NEW . Confirm Company / Financial Year / Month in the context bar. Click the refresh icon to (re)calculate from attendance and the salary structure. Review or adjust cells if required. Click Save to commit the payroll for the period. What is deducted automatically Deduction Source PF Employee's PF rate on the PF-flagged heads, capped at the configured wage limit VPF Employee's voluntary PF percentage ESI Applied when gross is within the ESI threshold Professional Tax Employee and designation PT settings TDS Configurable income-tax slabs Loan EMI Any Active loan in Loan Setup User Defined Deductions Active custom deductions Deduction-type salary heads NEW Shown in the grid's Head Ded. column and on the deductions side of the payslip LOP Pr"},{"t":"Guide: 9. Payroll Processing / 9.3 Bulk update of a salary head NEW","x":"Tick the employees in the Net Pay grid; the Bulk Update Head button appears. Choose the salary head and enter the amount. Select whether to Set the value or Add to the current value, then apply. Alternatively use Import Excel in the same window to load per-employee amounts from a spreadsheet."},{"t":"Guide: 9. Payroll Processing / 9.4 Toolbar actions","x":"Cal TDS - recalculate TDS for every row. Transfer TDS - mark the period's TDS as remitted, for records. Challan - PDF summary of total PF, ESI, Professional Tax and TDS for statutory deposit. Clear Col - clear one chosen column across all rows before re-entering. Export - Net Pay to Excel; Payslips shortcut to download payslips. Challan and Form 16 are computed from your payroll records for convenience. Always verify figures before filing."},{"t":"Guide: 10. Payslips & Payslip Designer / 10.1 Payslips UPDATED","x":"Payroll > Payslips lists every processed payslip for the period. The redesigned payslip shows the company logo (prominent) with a modest company name, income and deduction heads, loan details, amount in words and a footer disclaimer. Click a row to preview ; then Download PDF , Download Word or Print . Tick several employees for the Bulk Export Wizard - many employees and months in one ZIP. Email Selected NEW - tick employees and click it to email each their payslip as a PDF attachment (Section 15)."},{"t":"Guide: 10. Payslips & Payslip Designer / 10.2 Payslip Designer NEW","x":"Masters > Payslip Designer is an optional drag-and-drop editor for your own payslip layout. The standard layout is used until you save a design. Click a field in the left list to add it to the page, or add free text. Drag an element to move it; use the bottom-right handle to resize. In the property panel set exact X / Y / Width / Height (mm), font, size, weight, alignment and colour, and whether the field shows a label. Click Live Preview to see it with a real saved payroll record. Click Save . Use Reset to Default to return to the built-in layout, or Remove from payslip to delete the selected element. Saved designs apply to the Payslips screen, Net Pay downloads and bulk ZIP exports alike - all use one shared payslip generator."},{"t":"Guide: 11. Reports & Form 16","x":"Reports > All Reports opens the Reports Center."},{"t":"Guide: 11. Reports & Form 16 / 11.1 Ready-made reports","x":"Report Description Employee Master List Active employees with personal and salary details Monthly Attendance Log Detailed daily attendance status Salary Sheet Monthly payroll with all heads and deductions PF & ESI Statement Contribution report Bank Advice Net-pay list for bank transfer TDS & Tax Report Tax deductions and projections Yearly Salary Register Annual summary per employee Department Summary Headcount and cost by department Reports filter by month, year and employee, and export to Excel/CSV."},{"t":"Guide: 11. Reports & Form 16 / 11.2 Form 16","x":"Select Form 16 in the Reports Center. Choose the Employee and Financial Year. Click Generate Form 16 PDF . This is a simplified system-generated certificate for internal use, drawn from saved payroll records - not a substitute for the statutory e-filed Form 16."},{"t":"Guide: 11. Reports & Form 16 / 11.3 Custom Report Builder","x":"Pick a data source (Employees, Payroll History, Attendance Logs), tick the columns (Select All / Deselect All), and export the resulting table."},{"t":"Guide: 12. Documents & Letters","x":"Documents > Letters generates offer, appointment and other letters by merging your templates with a selected employee's data. Create or edit a template ; insert placeholders using the tag buttons, for example {{name}} . Select the employee and the letter, then preview. Use Print , Download PDF / Word , or Email NEW to send it to the employee's registered address. Available tags include: Full/First/Last Name, Employee Code, Designation, Department, Branch, DOB, DOJ, Exit Date, Monthly Salary, Salary From, Father Name, Gender, Blood Group, Phone, Email, Full Address, City, PAN, Aadhaar, PF, ESI, UAN, Bank Name, Account No., IFSC, Emergency Contact, Company Name and Current Date. Two image tags, Signature and Photo , insert the employee's saved signature or photo. Reference-number prefix and sequencing are set in Settings > Document Config."},{"t":"Guide: 13. Other Modules & Availability","x":"Everything reachable from the ribbon is described in Sections 3 12 and 14 18. Two further points: Recruitment, Helpdesk, Performance and Assets screens. Earlier guides described these modules. In version 3.2 their screens are not connected to the ribbon or the Dashboard, so they cannot be opened from the application. If your organisation relies on them, contact your MpxHR implementation partner. Asset data is still available as a table you can export to and import from Google Sheets (Section 16) and view or correct in the DB Viewer (Section 18). Module visibility for Masters, Attendance, Payroll, Reports and Documents is controlled in Settings > Module Rights . Employee-role logins see only their own attendance, leave and payslips (Section 20)."},{"t":"Guide: 14. Importing Data & Files","x":"Employees and Attendance can be imported from Excel. Both now run a pre-import validation and show the findings in a preview window before anything is saved."},{"t":"Guide: 14. Importing Data & Files / 14.1 Steps","x":"Click Template (Employees) or Tpl (Attendance) to download the correct sheet layout, and fill it in. Click Import / Imp and choose the file. Read the preview : the row table plus a list of warnings and errors. If there are errors, tick the acknowledgement checkbox to unlock Import - or cancel, fix the sheet and try again. Warnings never block."},{"t":"Guide: 14. Importing Data & Files / 14.2 What is checked","x":"Import Checks Employees Duplicate Employee Code within the file; the same email on rows with different names; missing First Name; unreadable DOB or date of joining Attendance Unknown employee codes; unreadable dates; duplicate employee + date pairs; unrecognised status values; missing Employee Code or Status"},{"t":"Guide: 14. Importing Data & Files / 14.3 Good to know","x":"Dates are read as DD/MM/YYYY (and Excel date serial numbers) - never silently as US-style MM/DD. Employees sharing one email (a supervisor's, for example) are no longer merged : email only counts as a match when the first name also matches. Salary columns such as BasicSalary and SpecialAllowance import into the salary structure that payroll reads. Dropdown/Yes-No custom field values are trimmed and matched ignoring case. Payroll itself has no Excel import - PF, ESI, TDS and Net Pay are computed from settings and attendance. Only salary-head amounts can be loaded in bulk (Section 9.3)."},{"t":"Guide: 14. Importing Data & Files / 14.4 Photos, Signatures & Documents NEW","x":"Employee photos, signatures and documents (Aadhaar, PAN, certificates ...) can be added one at a time in the employee form, or in bulk with Masters > Employees > Import Files . Bulk import works from a local folder, an Excel sheet, or a Google Drive folder, and always shows a preview before anything is saved. One employee Photo and Signature : use the Browse buttons beside the employee form. The picture is checked against the current limits and scaled down if very large. Documents : open an existing employee, type a document type (or pick one from the list), click Upload File . Use the eye icon to open a document and the bin icon to delete it. Many employees - Import Files Click Import Files in the Employees toolbar and choose the source below. Click Preview . Every file is listed with the employee it matches, where it will go (Photo, Signature or Document: type), its size, and a note if"},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails","x":"MpxHR can email payslips and letters and send automatic notifications. It is configured once for the whole app at Masters > Settings > Email , where a built-in Setup Guide also explains each step."},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails / 15.1 Choose a provider","x":"Provider When to use SMTP server Recommended. Gmail, Outlook / Microsoft 365, Zoho, Yahoo or your company mail server. One-click presets fill host, port and security. Google account When SMTP or App Passwords are not possible. Uses the Google Sync script; no password is stored in MpxHR."},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails / 15.2 Gmail via SMTP","x":"In your Google Account > Security, turn on 2-Step Verification . Search App passwords , create one named MpxHR and copy the 16-letter code. In MpxHR click the Gmail preset. Username = full Gmail address; Password = the App Password (not your normal password). Fill From Name and From Email (use the same address), click Save Email Settings . Type your own address beside Send Test and click it. If it arrives, everything else will work. Outlook: use the Outlook / 365 preset (smtp.office365.com, port 587, STARTTLS); your IT admin may need to enable Authenticated SMTP for the mailbox. Other hosts: port 587 with STARTTLS, or 465 with SSL/TLS."},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails / 15.3 What can be emailed","x":"Email How it is sent Payslips Payslips screen tick employees Email Selected (PDF attached) Letters Letters screen choose employee and letter Email Leave decision Automatic on Approve / Reject, if the Automatic Emails box is ticked Birthday wishes Automatic, once a day when MpxHR is opened, if ticked Each employee needs a valid Email in their profile; others are skipped and listed as failed. Gmail limits a normal account to about 500 emails a day."},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails / 15.4 Email templates","x":"Edit subject and body for Payslip, Letter, Leave Approved, Leave Rejected and Birthday under Email Templates , then Save Templates . Placeholders are replaced when sending: Template Placeholders Payslip {name} {month} {company} Letter {name} {letter_type} {company} Leave approved / rejected {name} {leave_type} {from} {to} {days} {company} Birthday {name} {company}"},{"t":"Guide: 15. Email Setup & Automatic Emails / 15.5 Email troubleshooting","x":"Message Fix Invalid login / not accepted Gmail needs an App Password; check the username is the full address Connection timeout / ECONNREFUSED Wrong host/port or firewall; try 587 + STARTTLS or 465 + SSL/TLS Wrong version number / SSL error Security must match the port: 587 = STARTTLS, 465 = SSL/TLS Lands in spam Use a From Email matching the login account Unknown action: sendMail The deployed Google script is old - recopy and redeploy the latest one"},{"t":"Guide: 16. Google Sync & Form Builder","x":"Masters > Settings > Google Sync connects MpxHR to a Google Sheet through a small script that runs under your own Google account . There is no Google sign-in inside MpxHR, no Cloud project and nothing to install; the shared secret is stored encrypted on your PC."},{"t":"Guide: 16. Google Sync & Form Builder / 16.1 Connect a Sheet","x":"Click Connect a Sheet and follow the on-screen instructions to copy the script into Apps Script from your Sheet and deploy it. Paste the resulting web-app link and secret back into MpxHR. If you connected before email was added, recopy the latest script over the old one and redeploy so email sending works. Whenever MpxHR needs a newer script (for the Joiner Form or Google Forms) it opens a short guide: copy the script, paste it in Apps Script, Deploy > Manage deployments > pencil > New version , allow the permission, then press Check now . Never choose \"New deployment\": that changes your link."},{"t":"Guide: 16. Google Sync & Form Builder / 16.2 Table Sync","x":"Click New Sync to link a database table with a Sheet tab. Tables available: Employees, Departments, Designations, Attendance, Loans, Assets (and your custom tables). Syncs can be edited in place. Export - write a table to a tab. Import - rows pulled from the tab go to the Review Queue . Column mapping is guessed automatically and you can adjust it. A preview shows what a sync will do before it runs."},{"t":"Guide: 16. Google Sync & Form Builder / 16.3 Review Queue","x":"Nothing becomes a real record until you approve it. Each mapping gets its own table; cells with problems are highlighted amber with a warning icon (hover for the reason). Checked on import Behaviour Dates (DOB, joining) Read as DD/MM/YYYY and stored in a standard format; invalid values are flagged Duplicate keys in the same sheet Flagged on the row (for example, one email on two employees) instead of being silently skipped Employee last name Optional"},{"t":"Guide: 16. Google Sync & Form Builder / 16.4 Form Builder","x":"Design a Google Form from any table's fields - or link several tables (for example Employee + Loan) so one submission fills them all. Generate the form through the connected Sheet, share the link, and review incoming responses in a section-by-section preview before approving them into real records."},{"t":"Guide: 17. Custom Fields & Custom Tables","x":"Masters > Settings > Custom Fields lets you extend MpxHR without any code change."},{"t":"Guide: 17. Custom Fields & Custom Tables / 17.1 Add a field to an existing form","x":"Choose the Table (for example Employees). Enter a Label , choose a Type and mark it Required if needed. Click Add Field . It appears on that table's forms immediately. Type Use Text / Long Text Short or multi-line text Number Numeric value Date Date picker Yes / No Tick box Dropdown Fixed list - give comma-separated options, e.g. A, B, C File / Image Upload a document or picture"},{"t":"Guide: 17. Custom Fields & Custom Tables / 17.2 Create a new table","x":"Under Create New Table enter a name (for example Vendors or Training Records ) and click Create Table . Add fields to it as above, then add and view its Records directly on this screen. Existing fields can be edited, and custom tables can be deleted."},{"t":"Guide: 18. Settings Reference","x":"Masters > Settings has a left-hand menu of tabs: Tab What you configure General Theme and date-format preferences Branding Application name and logo shown across the app and on login Notifications Birthday and work-anniversary desktop notifications Salary Components Company-wide earning and deduction defaults Payroll & Leave Month start day, LOP basis, overtime multiplier, default probation days, LWF contribution and frequency, leave accrual rules, PL/CL monthly credit, RH annual quota Document Config Letter reference prefix and sequencing Database Maintenance Manual and automatic backups, restore (Section 19) DB Viewer NEW Administrator-only direct view and edit of any database table Email NEW Provider, automatic emails, templates (Section 15) Google Sync NEW Sheets, table syncs, review queue, Form Builder (Section 16) Custom Fields NEW Extra fields and tables (Section 17) License NEW T"},{"t":"Guide: 18. Settings Reference / DB Viewer","x":"Pick a table, search across all columns, page through rows and use Add Row or the row editor. It bypasses the validation of normal screens, so a wrong edit (for example an unhashed password) can break data - take a backup first and use it only for corrections you fully understand."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security","x":"Masters > Settings > Database Maintenance shows the date and contents of your last backup at the top. A card turns green when the last backup is recent and amber when it is a week old or more, or when none has been taken."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.1 Back up now","x":"Everything (data + documents) - a .zip with the database and every uploaded file (documents, joiner files). This is the safest choice. Data only - a compact .sqlite file with all records. Type a password first to save it encrypted (.enc). Remember the password: without it an encrypted backup cannot be opened. MpxHR takes a consistent copy of the database even while you are working, checks the file after saving, and tells you what it holds (for example \"44 employees, 1 company, 123 payroll rows\"). Save a copy on a pen drive or in a Google Drive / OneDrive folder, not only on this computer."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.2 Automatic backup","x":"Tick Back up automatically every time I close MpxHR , and optionally Also include uploaded documents . Save in folder - choose a folder (a Drive/OneDrive-synced one keeps a copy in the cloud). Open shows it in Windows. If the folder is not available (for example a pen drive that is unplugged) the backup is saved in a safe default folder instead of being lost. Keep the latest - how many automatic backups to keep (1 to 200). Older ones are deleted. Back up now to this folder makes an automatic-style backup immediately."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.3 Recent automatic backups","x":"The list shows the newest automatic backups with date and size. Click Restore on one to bring it back without browsing for a file."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.4 Restore from a file","x":"Click Choose a backup file (.zip, .sqlite or .enc) and type the password for an encrypted one. Restoring replaces all current data and documents. MpxHR first checks the file: the password, that it is a MpxHR database, and its integrity. A wrong password or a damaged file stops the restore and changes nothing. A safety copy of the data you had is saved in the backups > before-restore folder (the last five are kept), so a mistaken restore can be undone. Files from a zip are written only inside MpxHR's uploads folder. Afterwards MpxHR restarts so every screen loads the restored data."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.5 Where is my data?","x":"In the installed program the database is %APPDATA%\\mpxhr-desktop\\database.sqlite and the uploaded files are in the uploads folder beside it. Backups made with MpxHR 4.1.x or older did not reliably include the database, so after upgrading to 4.2 take a new Everything backup straight away. Take a fresh backup before restoring, before upgrading MpxHR and before any large import."},{"t":"Guide: 19. Backup, Restore & Data Security / 19.6 Built-in protection","x":"Passwords are stored hashed; the Google Sync secret is encrypted with the operating system's secure storage. Administrative actions (deleting records, restore, DB Viewer, raw queries) need an active administrator session. Only one copy of MpxHR can run at a time, protecting the database from write conflicts. Company data is isolated per company; activity is written to a local diagnostic log for support. Masters > Data Security opens a short in-app guide to these practices."},{"t":"Guide: 20. User Roles, Passwords & Recovery","x":"Role Access Administrator All modules, all employees' data, payroll, settings, backups, user management Employee Self-service: own attendance, leave application and payslips Create employee logins in Settings > Security & Users , linking each to an employee record."},{"t":"Guide: 20. User Roles, Passwords & Recovery / Changing the admin password","x":"In Security & Users type the new password twice and click Update Profile ."},{"t":"Guide: 20. User Roles, Passwords & Recovery / Master recovery password NEW","x":"An administrator can set a backup password that logs in as any user - enter the person's username as usual and the master password instead of theirs. It lets you recover access when someone forgets a password. Leave the field empty and save to remove it. The tab shows whether one is currently set. Keep the master password secret and private - anyone who knows it can sign in as any user."},{"t":"Guide: 21. Keyboard Shortcuts & Tips","x":"Shortcut Action Ctrl + S Save the current form (works while typing) Ctrl + N New record Ctrl + E Edit the selected record Del Delete the selected record(s) Ctrl + R Refresh the current screen Ctrl + P Print Esc Close the open dialog (works while typing) Alt + 1 4 Switch between the first four ribbon tabs Shortcuts other than Save and Esc are paused while your cursor is inside a text box. Click the keyboard icon in the title bar to see the list in the app."},{"t":"Guide: 21. Keyboard Shortcuts & Tips / Good habits","x":"Check the Company / Financial Year / Month in the context bar before every entry. Mark attendance completely (use Auto-Fill) before calculating payroll. Close a month once payroll is final. Back up before bulk deletes, imports, restores or DB Viewer edits. Preview imports carefully - fix errors in the sheet rather than overriding them."},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form","x":"Masters > Onboarding helps you receive a new person properly before an employee record exists: collect their details and documents, follow a joining checklist, and turn them into an employee with one click."},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.1 Add a new joiner","x":"Click New Joiner and enter the name, email, phone, department, designation, branch and expected joining date. Save. The standard joining checklist is created for that person (documents to collect, HR steps, IT and admin steps). The list shows each joiner with a progress bar and a status: Pending , In progress or Completed . The cards at the top count them."},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.2 The checklist","x":"Select a joiner and click Checklist (or double-click the row). Tick a step when it is done, or add and remove your own steps. The status changes by itself. Checklist Template edits the standard list. Write one step per line as Group | Task . It applies to new joiners; people already added keep their list. Restore default brings back the original steps. Print Form prints a joining form with blank lines for the joiner to fill by hand, plus the checklist, with signature lines."},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.3 Make Employee","x":"Select the joiner and click Make Employee . MpxHR creates the employee with the name, email, phone, company, branch, department, designation and joining date, ticks the \"Employee record created\" step, and copies everything the joiner sent through the form (see below): profile fields, custom fields, photo, signature and documents. Then open Masters > Employees to add the employee code, salary and the remaining details. The employee limit of your license applies as usual."},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.4 The Joiner Form (online link)","x":"Let the joiner fill in their own details and upload documents from a phone. It runs on your own Google Sheet script (the same one used by Google Sync, Section 16). MpxHR never stores your Google login. Choose the questions. Onboarding > Joiner Form > Questions & documents . Tick what the joiner should upload (photo, Aadhaar copy, PAN copy, bank proof, certificates, relieving letter ...) and fill in (PAN number, UAN, date of birth, address, bank details ...). Name, mobile, email, department, designation, joining date and notes are always asked. Tick Must fill for compulsory ones. You can also add your own question. Get the link. Click Get link / Share . The first time (and after an MpxHR update) a short five-step guide appears to paste the new script into your Google Sheet; the Check now button tells you which step is still missing. Then copy the link or send it by WhatsApp or email. Join"},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.5 Where each answer goes, checks and limits","x":"Open Options on a question to change the defaults, which are already sensible: Setting What it does Save the answer to Keep with the joiner only; an Employee profile field (PAN, Aadhaar, bank, address ...) or an Employee custom field; for files: the employee photo, signature or a document type. Applied when you click Make Employee . Check the answer is PAN (ABCDE1234F), Aadhaar (12 digits), IFSC, UAN (12 digits), PIN code (6 digits), mobile (10 digits), bank account (6 20 digits), email, letters only, digits only. Spaces are tidied and PAN/IFSC are made capital automatically. Longest answer, smallest / largest Limits for text length and number ranges. Dropdown answers must be one of the choices. Biggest file, allowed types Per file question, up to 5 MB (a Google script limit) and PDF, JPG, PNG or DOCX. A photo or signature can only be JPG or PNG. The limits in Settings > Files & Uploads "},{"t":"Guide: 22. Onboarding & the Joiner Form / 22.6 Google Form (advanced)","x":"In Onboarding > Joiner Form you can also build a real Google Form (Section 16). It asks the fixed joiner fields and its answers wait in the review queue. It needs the extra Google Forms permission in your script and cannot take file uploads , so the online link above is recommended. Forms have Preview (shows the questions as they will be asked) and Share (copy the link, send it by WhatsApp or email)."},{"t":"Guide: 23. Troubleshooting & Support","x":"Issue What to try Forgot a password Sign in with the master recovery password if one is set; otherwise contact your administrator or MpxHR support Payroll figures look wrong Check Financial Year / Month, make sure attendance is complete, confirm the salary structure and salary-head flags, then refresh/recalculate before saving A module is missing from the ribbon Check Settings > Module Rights Cannot open a second window By design - only one copy of MpxHR runs at a time Financial Year dropdown lacks a year It lists current year 4 to +1 and selects today's year automatically Import preview shows errors Fix duplicates, dates (DD/MM/YYYY) or unknown codes in the file and import again Emails fail Use Send Test in Settings > Email and see Section 15.5; confirm the employee has an Email on file Google Sync errors Make sure the latest script is deployed, the link and secret are correct, and you "}] };
